{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>et the table.</b> The holiness of the table is not equal to the holiness of that which precedes it; therefore it says <b>et</b>. And it says concerning all its components <b>ve'et</b>, for the level of all of them is equal in holiness. <b>Ve'et the menorah of the light</b> — with the addition of the letter vav, to say that its holiness and the holiness of its vessels are equal to the holiness of the table and its vessels. And it says <b>ve'et the golden altar</b> — likewise in the same category as the menorah and the table with its vessels, and the anointing oil, etc., up to the screen of the entrance — for every component the verse says <b>ve'et</b>, to say that all of them are in one category. And it says <b>et the altar of burnt offering</b> without a vav, to say that it is not in the category of holiness of what preceded it, and its position proves this. And it says <b>ve'et its grating</b> — which is in the same category as it. And it says <b>et its staves</b> — which are not in the same category as it. <b>Ve'et all its vessels</b> — in one category together with its staves. <b>Et the laver</b> — it is not in the category of the copper altar. <b>Ve'et its base</b> — in one category with the laver. <b>Et the hangings of the court</b> — they are not in the category of the altar of burnt offering and its vessels. <b>Et its pillars</b> — a category below the hangings. <b>Ve'et their sockets and et the screen</b> — in one category with its pillars. <b>Et the pegs</b> — a category unto itself. <b>Ve'et the pegs of the court and et their cords</b> — all are equal in one category. <b>Et the garments of service</b> — they are things that cover the holy objects during travel, and their level is below the level of the pegs, etc. <b>Et the holy garments</b> — they are a level unto themselves. And see what I wrote in parashat Terumah (Exodus 25:7), that one does not commit sacrilege (me'ilah) with the priestly garments, whereas one does commit sacrilege with all the sacred vessels. <b>Ve'et the garments of his sons</b> — they are equal to the holiness of the garments of Aharon their father; therefore it joined them with a connecting vav."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:36:53.875417773Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}